OL,3,CNo solar eclipse glasses? Here are
OL,4,Cfive ways to watch it safely
OL,6,FWhat happens if I look at the eclipse
OL,7,Fwithout eye protection?
OL,9,FThe UK Health Security Agency (UKHSA)
OL,10,Fwarns of the risk of retina damage if
OL,11,Fviewers look into the Sun without
OL,12,Fadequate protection.
OL,14,FAn eclipse makes the Sun appear
OL,15,Fdimmer, meaning you may be tempted to
OL,16,Fcatch a glimpse with the naked eye.
OL,18,FHowever, this can override the body's
OL,19,Fnatural reflex to look away, allowing
OL,20,Fintense sunlight to enter and damage
OL,21,Fthe retina.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
