PN,31412
SC,0012
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786491135
OL,3,CNo solar eclipse glasses? Here are
OL,4,Cfive ways to watch it safely
OL,6,FCrucially, the retina has no pain
OL,7,Freceptors, so you will not feel the
OL,8,Fdamage as it happens.
OL,10,FData from the Royal College of
OL,11,FOphthalmologists shows there were
OL,12,Faround 70 cases of vision problems
OL,13,Ffollowing the 1999 solar eclipse, with
OL,14,Faround 40% viewing it for less than a
OL,15,Fminute.
OL,17,FDo sunglasses work just as well?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G12/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31413
SC,0013
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F314A1786491135
OL,3,CNo solar eclipse glasses? Here are
OL,4,Cfive ways to watch it safely
OL,6,FThe UKHSA says sunglasses or 3D
OL,7,Fglasses will not adequately protect
OL,8,Fyour eyes and should not be used as a
OL,9,Freplacement for eclipse glasses or
OL,10,Fhandheld solar viewers.
OL,12,FAlthough they reduce glare, they do
OL,13,Fnot stop harmful solar radiation from
OL,14,Fhitting the eyes.
OL,16,FThe solar eclipse can be spotted
OL,17,Facross the UK from 6pm until 8pm on
OL,18,FWednesday, and is set to peak between
OL,19,F7.05pm and 7.16pm, depending on
OL,20,Flocation.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G13/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
